# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values to switch the
# "Scripts de Reunião" / "Reuniões" persistence layer from localStorage to
# Supabase. VITE_SUPABASE_URL + a client-safe key are required together — if
# either is missing, the app automatically falls back to localStorage (see
# src/store/index.ts) and keeps working with no crash.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Create a Supabase project (or use the one already created for ABZA).
#   2. Run the migrations in supabase/migrations/, in order, against it
#      (SQL Editor, one file at a time — or `supabase db push` if you adopt
#      the CLI later).
#   3. Project Settings > API > "Publishable key" (the current key name —
#      Supabase projects created before this naming still show "anon
#      public", which is the same kind of client-safe key under the old
#      name). Copy the Project URL and that key.
#   4. Set them below, in .env.local (never commit real values).
#
# These are read at build time by Vite and end up in the client bundle —
# that's expected for this key class (RLS is what actually protects the
# data, not keeping this key secret). NEVER put the "secret key" /
# service_role key here or anywhere in this repo — that one bypasses RLS
# entirely and must only ever live server-side (this project doesn't use it
# anywhere today).

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY= — legacy name, still read as a fallback if you have
# an older Supabase project that only shows "anon public" instead of
# "Publishable key". Use PUBLISHABLE_KEY above for any new setup.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ABZA Sales Copilot — OpenAI (server-side only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Usada exclusivamente por api/copilot.ts, lida via process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY.
# NUNCA prefixe com VITE_ — isso a colocaria no bundle público do frontend.
# Configure na Vercel em Project Settings > Environment Variables (não em
# .env.local se você também usa `vite dev` com um proxy público; para rodar
# localmente use um .env.local não commitado, ou exporte no shell antes de
# `npm run test:copilot` / `vercel dev`).
#
# OPENAI_MODEL é opcional — se omitida, usa o padrão definido em api/copilot.ts.

OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=
